1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,945
If teleportation
exists,

2
00:00:01,965 --> 00:00:04,245
why are merchants
still using horses?

3
00:00:04,265 --> 00:00:05,662
Here,
a crystal gate links

4
00:00:05,682 --> 00:00:06,836
two cities.

5
00:00:06,856 --> 00:00:08,690
Each jump burns a
crystal worth more

6
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:09,740
than the cargo.

7
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,073
It reaches one city.

8
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:12,932
Every village needs
the road.

9
00:00:12,952 --> 00:00:14,856
One jump in a
hundred fails.

10
00:00:14,876 --> 00:00:16,799
The guild rations
the rest.

11
00:00:16,819 --> 00:00:18,761
So it carries only
what can't wait:

12
00:00:18,781 --> 00:00:20,845
medicine,
royal mail.

13
00:00:20,865 --> 00:00:22,932
Magic doesn't
replace technology.

14
00:00:22,952 --> 00:00:24,295
Price,
range and

15
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:26,770
reliability decide
who uses what.

16
00:00:26,790 --> 00:00:28,669
What technology
would magic replace

17
00:00:28,689 --> 00:00:30,269
first in your world?
